it took me longer than I thought to write some additional documentation =
but
now I can proudly present the first real usage of the galley stuff =
(though the
module actually predates the galley implementation; back then it did all =
the
parshape handling manually in the template :-)

you will find on www.latex-project.org/code/experimental
the file xinitials.tgz (and the directory xinitials)

it contains:

 xinitials.dtx  the template definition, document interface ...
 xinitials.ins  the usual unpacker
 xinitials-test.tex       a test file

to run it you also need the files from the directory galley (ie galley2 =
and
xhj)

hope you agree with me that playing with the initials is fun, though not
really a very serious application. For that you'll have to wait for
xlists.dtx.

have fun
frank

